+-- ============================================================================
+-- EMERGENCY SECURITY HOTFIX · market_listings view exposure
+-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+-- INCIDENT (read-only audit, 2026-09-03): three public views expose market_listings
+-- scraped data to anon + ordinary authenticated users, bypassing the frozen_view
+-- RLS (all are security_invoker=false and granted to anon/authenticated):
+--   * v_market_properties      — selects the FULL ml.data (contact info + source_payload). NO app/API/website consumer.
+--   * v_market_listings        — auto-generated typed BI view; exposes ALL columns incl. source_payload + advertiser_phone. NO app/API/website consumer.
+--   * market_listings_summary  — exposes advertiser_phone + deed/permit (NOT source_payload). CONSUMER: authenticated SPA (slim store / ContactAdvertiserPanel) — a PROVEN internal requirement.
+-- The two website views v_our_projects_scope / v_website_public were checked and do
+-- NOT return market_listings rows (they filter to the projects model) — untouched.
+--
+-- FIX (least privilege; no proven consumer loses access):
+--   v_market_properties / v_market_listings → revoke anon + authenticated + PUBLIC (no consumer); set security_invoker=true (defense in depth). Admin access, if ever needed, via a future admin RPC — not a broad grant.
+--   market_listings_summary → revoke anon + PUBLIC only; KEEP authenticated (the SPA). It stays the intended internal market-intelligence surface (advertiser_phone by design; source_payload already excluded).
+--
+-- No safe public projection is created because NO public/anon consumer exists.
+-- This hotfix is standalone and may apply independently BEFORE Gate A 01–05.
+-- SYSTEMIC FOLLOW-UP (separate, flagged): the auto-view generator (regenerate_model_view)
+--   grants anon/authenticated + security_invoker=false on EVERY frozen model's v_<name>
+--   view, so v_market_listings will be re-exposed on the next model change. A durable
+--   platform fix must patch the generator (invoker=true and/or no anon grant for
+--   sensitive models). Tracked outside this hotfix; the revoke below closes it now.
+-- ============================================================================
+
+BEGIN;
+
+-- v_market_properties: no consumer → remove app access + invoker=true.
+ALTER VIEW public.v_market_properties SET (security_invoker = true);
+REVOKE ALL ON public.v_market_properties FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;
+GRANT SELECT ON public.v_market_properties TO service_role;   -- infra only
+
+-- v_market_listings (auto BI view): no consumer → remove app access + invoker=true.
+DO $$ BEGIN
+  IF to_regclass('public.v_market_listings') IS NOT NULL THEN
+    EXECUTE 'ALTER VIEW public.v_market_listings SET (security_invoker = true)';
+    EXECUTE 'REVOKE ALL ON public.v_market_listings FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated';
+    EXECUTE 'GRANT SELECT ON public.v_market_listings TO service_role';
+  END IF;
+END $$;
+
+-- market_listings_summary: keep the authenticated SPA consumer; remove anon only.
+REVOKE ALL ON public.market_listings_summary FROM PUBLIC, anon;
+GRANT SELECT ON public.market_listings_summary TO authenticated, service_role;
+
+COMMIT;
+
+-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+-- Verification (run manually per role; not executed by this migration):
+--   docs/market-ingest/hotfix-tests.sql contains the anon / salesperson / admin /
+--   service_role assertions and expected results.
+-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
